MID_EV14_034_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_034_m01_001: Leda! Oh, I'm so glad to see you.
MID_EV14_034_m01_002: Oh, hello, Aswan! I didn't expect to see you here.
MID_EV14_034_m01_003: Actually, I've returned here a few times hoping\nI might run into you again.
MID_EV14_034_m01_004: Huh? This place isn't exactly reputable. You didn't\nrun into trouble, did you?
MID_EV14_034_m01_005: Some not very nice people are more than happy to\ntarget a nice girl like you...as you may remember.
MID_EV14_034_m01_006: I do have some martial training. I can take care of\nmyself as long as I have a weapon.
MID_EV14_034_m01_007: I know I shouldn't be going out like this, but I had\nto thank you.
MID_EV14_034_m01_008: You seem so mild-mannered and demure, but deep\ndown you're very driven, aren't you?
MID_EV14_034_m01_009: Oh, I have to tell you—I was in the audience for your\nlast match.
MID_EV14_034_m01_010: I was so surprised—I had no idea you were taking\npart in the Heroic Games!
MID_EV14_034_m01_011: I wasn't keeping it a secret or anything...but I am a\nbit embarrassed now that I know you were there.
MID_EV14_034_m01_012: Don't be! It was a wonderful match!
MID_EV14_034_m01_013: But Leda, I must admit I have a favor to ask.\nI wonder...would you play for me again?
MID_EV14_034_m01_014: <NCA>Accept her request.
MID_EV14_034_m01_015: <NCB>Feign reluctance.
MID_EV14_034_m01_016: <ACA>For you, I'd be delighted. What kind of song would\nyou like to hear?
MID_EV14_034_m01_017: <ACB>If you like my playing that much, perhaps I should\ncharge you for today's performance.
MID_EV14_034_m01_018: <ACB>Oh, uh...I don't have much money on hand. I do have\nthis hairpin. Perhaps that would suffice?
MID_EV14_034_m01_019: <ACB>I'm just kidding. I don't want your money. But I do\nwant to know what kind of song you'd like.
MID_EV14_034_m01_020: Let me think... How about a song in which the two\nprotagonists eventually find their happy ending?
MID_EV14_034_m01_021: Hmm...ah! I have one for you. I'll play a song about\nthe Seven Labors of Arago.
MID_EV14_034_m01_022: In this legend, Olivia's carriage breaks down and can\ngo no further. So Arago lifts it onto his shoulders...
MID_EV14_034_m01_023: and carries it over a mountain pass. And in the end,\nhe marries her.
MID_EV14_034_m01_024: And so the story ends.
MID_EV14_034_m01_025: What a moving performance that was. I somehow\nfeel more courageous just from listening to it.
MID_EV14_034_m01_026: I'm so glad I played it for you, then.
MID_EV14_034_m01_027: That story is about an ancestor of mine, so I've heard\nit many times since I was a child.
MID_EV14_034_m01_028: But the version of the story in your song...it affects\nme in such a different way.
MID_EV14_034_m01_029: Wait, the hero—Arago—is your ancestor? Aswan,\nI don't understand... Who are you?
MID_EV14_034_m01_030: I'm sorry I've kept this from you for so long, Leda.
MID_EV14_034_m01_031: I am Aswan Hasdrubal Aragon. I am King Gilchris\nof Arago's...queen.
MID_EV14_034_m01_032: You're...the queen of Arago? What are you doing in\na place like this?
MID_EV14_034_m01_033: I told you before about the person I so very much\nwant to save.
MID_EV14_034_m01_034: He and I were once engaged to be married. But he\nwas framed for the murder of the king.
MID_EV14_034_m01_035: He has been imprisoned here in Dagsion as if he\nwere the most vile criminal.
MID_EV14_034_m01_036: And I...I want to do something. I want to rescue him.
MID_EV14_034_m01_037: But I have precious few allies, Leda. And so\nI thought that if you'd be willing, perhaps...
MID_EV14_034_m01_038: Wait a minute. This person you are trying to save...\nWhat's his name?
MID_EV14_034_m01_039: Oh, yes. His name is Bertrand. He has also become\nknown as the White-Maned Demon in the arena.
MID_EV14_034_m01_040: Tch!
MID_EV14_034_m01_041: Never show your face to me again! Do you\nunderstand? I never want to see you again!
MID_EV14_034_m01_042: Leda? What's gotten into you all of a sudden?!
MID_EV14_034_m01_043: I can't believe this. Aswan is his ex-fiancée?\nWhat kind of twisted joke is this?
MID_EV14_034_m01_044: And I was just sitting there talking to her like...\nlike we're best friends.
MID_EV14_035_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_035_m01_001: Did you notice there's no wind tonight? You should\nbe careful on evenings like these.
MID_EV14_035_m01_002: This again? Are you still spying on me?
MID_EV14_035_m01_003: It's a coincidence we crossed paths, I assure you.\nA lady I've been pursuing stood me up. So here I am.
MID_EV14_035_m01_004: You're terrible, you know that? I don't understand\nhow you do this day in and day out.
MID_EV14_035_m01_005: It doesn't matter. What matters is what you're up to.\nAre you off to practice summoning the Phantom?
MID_EV14_035_m01_006: It isn't good for you, Leda. You should stop.
MID_EV14_035_m01_007: That's not where I'm going. I want to peek into the\nguesthouse where the group from Arago is staying.
MID_EV14_035_m01_008: I figure I might have a chance to kill Lechner while\nI'm at it.
MID_EV14_035_m01_009: You should not. It would be reckless in the extreme.
MID_EV14_035_m01_010: Those Aragonian soldiers aren't there for show. Plus,\nI hear the Twin Jewels of Arago are on hand too.
MID_EV14_035_m01_011: Even if you did manage it, you'd create an ugly\nincident at a temple facility.
MID_EV14_035_m01_012: Something like that... Even my lady Kalla could not\nprotect you.
MID_EV14_035_m01_013: Besides, you've caught the scent of a bigger and more\nimportant conspiracy behind all of this, no?
MID_EV14_035_m01_014: More and more, Lechner and his ilk seem like minor\nplayers in a much bigger scheme.
MID_EV14_035_m01_015: Fine. But I still think it's worth checking the\nplace out.
MID_EV14_035_m01_016: No. I don't think it is. I've been mulling over a\nfragrance...ambergris from the southern sea...
MID_EV14_035_m01_017: Gods, Sirocco, what is that supposed to mean?
MID_EV14_035_m01_018: I'm sorry, but even I'm not yet sure. I will tell you\nonce these elusive thoughts take solid form.
MID_EV14_035_m01_019: Still, you must understand—your face is known to\nthem. You shouldn't wander around carelessly.
MID_EV14_035_m01_020: I can't sit around and do nothing. I just can't.
MID_EV14_035_m01_021: Listen—that man we saw with the bandages...\nI believe he's the key.
MID_EV14_035_m01_022: We must find a way to get access to him again.
MID_EV14_035_m01_023: There's no way he'll be taking deliveries in the same\nplace as last time—not after what happened.
MID_EV14_035_m01_024: And Lechner will be on alert. He'll make sure we\ndon't follow him to whatever new location they pick.
MID_EV14_035_m01_025: The ghost carriage will still arrive somewhere in the\nvicinity of Dagsion on the night of the new moon.
MID_EV14_035_m01_026: But yes, after our encounter with Lechner, they're\nsure to change the location of the deliveries.
MID_EV14_035_m01_027: Lake Baal is enormous. There are so many places\nthey could meet.
MID_EV14_035_m01_028: Miss Leda, do you remember the time we came\nacross the ghost carriage on the road?
MID_EV14_035_m01_029: <NCA>Remember the moment.
MID_EV14_035_m01_030: Yes. We were coming from Cohen's Mausoleum on\nour way to Kalla's temple.
MID_EV14_035_m01_031: The route from there to Dagsion is quite narrow,\nespecially for the ghost carriage.
MID_EV14_035_m01_032: You saw how large that carriage is. I doubt it could\ntravel the steep roads of the Midea Mountain Range.
MID_EV14_035_m01_033: That means they'd drive it by way of Fort Galcar\nand follow the river along the Talto Highway.
MID_EV14_035_m01_034: They'd have to cross the Santana Bridge to make\nsure they arrived in Dagsion by the new moon.
MID_EV14_035_m01_035: So my proposal is this... We ambush them at the\nSantana Bridge and seize the ghost carriage.
MID_EV14_035_m01_036: Seize...the ghost carriage?
MID_EV14_035_m01_037: Indeed. We'll hide the ghost carriage somewhere...\nand they'll have no choice but to come to us.
MID_EV14_035_m01_038: We might also get the chance to force the bandaged\nman to reveal his identity.
MID_EV14_035_m01_039: And of course I'd also like to take a look inside the\ncarriage. I'm very keen to know what the cargo is.
MID_EV14_035_m01_040: It's an interesting plan. If we have his precious cargo,\nLechner will have no choice but to do as we say.
MID_EV14_035_m01_041: But Sirocco, are you going to tell Kalla about\nthis plan?
MID_EV14_035_m01_042: Of course not—she would only try to stop us from\ndoing something so dangerous. This is our secret.
MID_EV14_104_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_104_m01_001: Miss Leda, you said before that you were a guest of\nFather Mahdel's.
MID_EV14_104_m01_002: Yes. Buccar and I went to him in 1445. He hid us\nfor about three years.
MID_EV14_104_m01_003: You said that he told you someone was holding\nhis family hostage.
MID_EV14_104_m01_004: You're sure that's what he said, yes? Is there any\nchance you heard him wrong?
MID_EV14_104_m01_005: No. No chance. Why do you ask?
MID_EV14_104_m01_006: I did some research on him and found something\nodd. Father Mahdel did not have a family.
MID_EV14_104_m01_007: What? Even if it is true, I don't understand what\nit means.
MID_EV14_104_m01_008: I can't say for sure. But it does bother me.
MID_EV14_104_m01_009: Why would Father Mahdel lie to you about that?
MID_EV14_104_m01_010: *sigh*
MID_EV14_104_m01_011: Miss Leda...the father is supposed to have served the\ntemple of Solel as high priest for a long time.
MID_EV14_104_m01_012: He then lost his position because of a scandal and\nwent into hiding around 1441. That's not so long ago.
MID_EV14_104_m01_013: You think there should be plenty of people in this\ncity who still remember him.
MID_EV14_104_m01_014: Exactly. I'd like to see what kind of information\nI can gather about Mahdel.
MID_EV14_104_m01_015: And I'd like your help, Miss Leda. I want you to\ncanvass the city...
MID_EV14_104_m01_016: Once you've gathered enough information,\ncome find me.
MID_EV14_104_m01_017: But why do you suspect him, of all people?
MID_EV14_104_m01_018: It's not that I suspect him—it's just this lie of his\nkeeps tugging at my mind.
MID_EV14_104_m01_019: I feel something lurking there...something that feels\ntied to this entire series of events.
MID_EV14_104_m01_020: I suppose I can't say no to you when you put it\nlike that.
MID_EV14_104_m01_021: It doesn't feel good to do this, but I'll see what\nI can find out.
MID_EV14_105_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_105_m01_001: You gathered far more intel than I expected.\nWell done, Miss Leda.
MID_EV14_105_m01_002: Based on what we've discovered so far...
MID_EV14_105_m01_003: It seems Father Mahdel had reason to, at\nthe very least, resent Viceroy Guillermo.
MID_EV14_105_m01_004: I never knew about any of what happened between\nmy parents and Father Mahdel.
MID_EV14_105_m01_005: It's interesting that their friendship survived, even\nafter your father left Dagsion.
MID_EV14_105_m01_006: It's also...interesting...that Father Mahdel never had\na family, just like you said.
MID_EV14_105_m01_007: But what I don't understand is...why would he\nlie about it?
MID_EV14_105_m01_008: Let me ask you this, Miss Leda... Did you ever see\nFather Mahdel's corpse—after he died in the fire?
MID_EV14_105_m01_009: Yes. It's like I told you—we found his corpse burned\nso badly that he was...unrecognizable...
MID_EV14_105_m01_010: So, you're saying that you cannot, in fact, confirm\nwhether Father Mahdel lived or died?
MID_EV14_105_m01_011: <NCA>Ask a question.
MID_EV14_105_m01_012: What are you getting at, Sirocco?
MID_EV14_105_m01_013: Think about it a moment. Let's say, for the sake of\nargument, a person was going to commit suicide...
MID_EV14_105_m01_014: Why would they lie to their best friend's daughter?\nEven if they had mixed feelings toward her.
MID_EV14_105_m01_015: *gasp*
MID_EV14_105_m01_016: Had he been truly repentant like he said he was in\nthat moment...then he would have told the truth.
MID_EV14_105_m01_017: Instead, he lied about having a family in danger...\nknowing full well that would forgive his sins.
MID_EV14_105_m01_018: I don't understand. I know what I saw... He was\nright in front of me at the time.
MID_EV14_105_m01_019: Look, all we know is that there's something more to\nFather Mahdel's story. Let's call it enough for today.
MID_EV14_105_m01_020: Those of us at Kalla's temple will need to continue\nlooking into things.
MID_EV14_105_m01_021: I'm just...still not sure I can bring myself to\nsuspect him.
MID_EV14_105_m01_022: Miss Leda, I believe that every one of us\nhas secrets.
MID_EV14_105_m01_023: And having secrets does not necessarily make\na person evil.
MID_EV14_105_m01_024: There's both good and bad within all of us.\nIt's just part of being human.
MID_EV14_105_m01_025: There are no purely good people...not in this world.
MID_EV14_105_m01_026: And while a person may be considered virtuous by\nsome, they may also be thought of as evil by others.
MID_EV14_105_m01_027: So even if Father Mahdel really does have\na dark side...
MID_EV14_105_m01_028: The good Father Mahdel who took care of you can\nalso still be real. Don't forget that.
MID_EV14_105_m01_029: You're right. Heh. I didn't expect that you, of all\npeople, could console me. Thank you.
MID_EV14_036_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_036_m01_001: Do you think it'll be here soon? We've been\nwaiting forever.
MID_EV14_036_m01_002: It feels like the ghost carriage is never gonna\nshow up.
MID_EV14_036_m01_003: I hope we haven't picked the wrong place for\nour ambush.
MID_EV14_036_m01_004: This is the only location that makes sense.\nIt will be here shortly.
MID_EV14_036_m01_005: He may spend too much time chasing skirts, but his\ninsights are not to be underestimated.
MID_EV14_036_m01_006: Hm. Is that right.
MID_EV14_036_m01_007: Just make sure you're ready to stop them when\nthey arrive.
MID_EV14_036_m01_008: Leave that to me. The plan is sound and we're ready.
MID_EV14_036_m01_009: <NCA>Listen carefully.
MID_EV14_036_m01_010: Wait—quiet. I hear a carriage in the distance.\nIt sounds...large.
MID_EV14_036_m01_011: Yes. Just as I thought. It's time.
MID_EV14_036_m01_012: Why have we stopped? What the hell is going on?!
MID_EV14_036_m01_013: Sir! There's a carriage blocking the road.
MID_EV14_036_m01_014: This is ridiculous. Get it out of the road NOW!
MID_EV14_036_m01_015: Ah. You!
MID_EV14_036_m01_016: Me. I'm here. You're here. What a coincidence. A bit\nearly for the new moon though. Something amiss?
MID_EV14_036_m01_017: Just as I thought. You adjusted your travel timing\nafter our previous attack.
MID_EV14_036_m01_018: So, the same losers who fled with tails between legs\nlast time have decided to return. Did you not learn?
MID_EV14_036_m01_019: Ah, but we did. We're far from Dagsion, are we\nnot? How will you call for help this time? Do tell.
MID_EV14_036_m01_020: Here's what I can tell you... Anyone who tries to\ntouch this cargo will not leave here with their lives.
MID_EV14_036_m01_021: In fact, I'm not gonna let any of you bastards\nlive, period.
MID_EV14_036_m01_022: I don't care about your cargo. Killing you is the\nonly thing that matters to me.
MID_EV14_036_m01_023: You know what you did to Kassite that day.
MID_EV14_036_m01_024: No idea what you're talking about. Lots of people\nhate me. I can never remember what I did to who.
MID_EV14_036_m01_025: Though, hold on—you mentioned Kassite last time,\ndidn't you?
MID_EV14_036_m01_026: Oh right, I remember now. You're the daughter\nof that viceroy. The kid who took pity on me.
MID_EV14_036_m01_027: If only you'd ratted me out to a grown-up instead. All\nthose bad things never would've happened to Kassite.
MID_EV14_036_m01_028: Yes. That's my sin, and I take responsibility for it.
MID_EV14_036_m01_029: Oh, you do, eh? Well then, I've got something to\nshow you.
MID_EV14_036_m01_030: Ohhh... Th-that's...
MID_EV14_036_m01_031: What have you done?! Lord Guillermo...
MID_EV14_036_m01_037: Why...why would you do such a horrible thing?!
MID_EV14_036_m01_041: I won't let you get away with this... I will kill you\nhere and now even if I have to sacrifice myself.
MID_EV14_036_m01_042: Oho. Whoa, so intense. She's trying to get in\nmy head.
MID_EV14_036_m01_043: They call me Mad Dog for a reason, little girl!\nI won't be intimidated by you.
MID_EV14_036_m01_044: You're going to lose, Lechner. Will you need to be\nrescued? What do you think?
MID_EV14_036_m01_045: You're gonna help me, are you? That's a surprise.
MID_EV14_036_m01_046: I was planning to watch the show from the shadows,\nbut it seems I have no choice but to get involved.
MID_EV14_036_m01_047: You...you're Maria! But why...why would you\nhelp him?!
MID_EV14_036_m01_048: I'm so very sorry. I really had grown fond of you,\nyou know.
MID_EV14_036_m01_049: But you bad little children have come for our cargo,\nso I simply cannot let you leave with your lives.
MID_EV14_036_m01_050: Really, you've been much too mischievous, my Rose\nof Caelus. It's a pity, but it's time to die.
MID_EV14_037_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_037_m01_001: I can't believe it. Beaten by this lot. Well, that's that.\nTime to ditch the cargo and get out of here.
MID_EV14_037_m01_002: Agreed. As loath as I am to do it, it would seem\nprudent to retreat and regroup.
MID_EV14_037_m01_003: You've backed me deep into a corner. I'll admit\nI may have underestimated you.
MID_EV14_037_m01_004: I suppose I should have expected as much from the\none chosen by Obsidian. Vexing, yet here we are.
MID_EV14_037_m01_005: But first, Lechner, I believe it is time for you to exit\nthe stage.
MID_EV14_037_m01_006: Huh?! What the hell is that supposed to mean?
MID_EV14_037_m01_007: Huh?! Urgh... Agh...
MID_EV14_037_m01_008: Lechner! Maria, why would you do that?!
MID_EV14_037_m01_009: I don't get it. I thought you were allies!
MID_EV14_037_m01_010: Dirty snake. You betrayed me...
MID_EV14_037_m01_011: You must understand. You've been a nuisance to\neveryone for quite some time now.
MID_EV14_037_m01_012: If only you'd been content with the coin we let you\nline your pockets with.
MID_EV14_037_m01_013: But no, you were greedy and failed to understand\nyour station. It's a sin I simply can't forgive.
MID_EV14_037_m01_014: Of course, I was planning to get rid of you eventually.
MID_EV14_037_m01_015: Damn you... Go to...hell...
MID_EV14_037_m01_016: Alas, the underworld is not my destination.
MID_EV14_037_m01_017: Wait! No! Give that to me!
MID_EV14_037_m01_018: I had intended to look the other way...out of respect\nfor your ancestor.
MID_EV14_037_m01_019: But you, knowing so very little of my true feelings,\ncrossed a line that should not have been crossed.
MID_EV14_037_m01_020: So, I won't be lavishing any more kindnesses\nupon you.
MID_EV14_037_m01_021: In truth, you deserve a good punishing. But you seem\nto have me at a disadvantage right now...
MID_EV14_037_m01_022: It's a shame, but I'll have to excuse myself for\nthe night.
MID_EV14_037_m01_023: Surely you don't think we're going to let you\nwalk away.
MID_EV14_037_m01_024: Oh, but I do. You can't catch me, you silly boy.
MID_EV14_037_m01_025: Mmph... What's...happening...
MID_EV14_037_m01_026: I can't... The strength...is leaving...my body...
MID_EV14_037_m01_027: No! A spellsong...a powerful one...
MID_EV14_037_m01_028: That vihuela...it belonged to the Virtuosa of Heaven\nand Earth... One of Drake's treasures...like Obsidian...
MID_EV14_106_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_106_m01_001: Well, well. Don't you look like you're having fun.\nSeems I joined this party at just the right time.
MID_EV14_106_m01_002: You?! Why, exactly, do you keep turning up?!
MID_EV14_106_m01_003: Talimun?! What are you doing here?!
MID_EV14_106_m01_004: Hey now. This is a coincidence, I assure you.
MID_EV14_106_m01_005: I got a tip from a friend that a strange carriage\nhas been coming and going through these parts.
MID_EV14_106_m01_006: I thought about which route I'd take a carriage\nthrough, if it were me... And here we are.
MID_EV14_106_m01_007: I figured whatever treasures they carry must be good,\nso I followed my trusty compass all the way here.
MID_EV14_106_m01_008: Yet I find myself arriving too late. And what's more...\nI've been beaten by people I know—more than one!
MID_EV14_106_m01_009: Wait...you know this woman too?
MID_EV14_106_m01_010: You could say that. We seem to be running into each\nother recently.
MID_EV14_106_m01_011: Seems this beauty and I are bound together by fate's\nred thread.
MID_EV14_106_m01_012: You overstep! Who would bind themselves\nto the likes of you?!
MID_EV14_106_m01_013: Hmm. Sounds like she hates you quite a bit.
MID_EV14_106_m01_014: If I may change the subject...it seems the spellsong\nhasn't affected you in the slightest.
MID_EV14_106_m01_015: Hm? Oh, now that you mention it...you're right.\nI feel fine. How curious...
MID_EV14_106_m01_016: {SetColor=Gray}Just as I thought. My spellsongs won't be as effective\non this man...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_106_m01_017: {SetColor=Gray}Tch. How did I end up with this joke for a...a... Ugh.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_106_m01_029: If I may change the subject...it seems the spellsong\nhasn't affected you in the slightest.
MID_EV14_106_m01_030: Hm? Oh, now that you mention it...you're right.\nI feel fine. How curious...
MID_EV14_106_m01_031: {SetColor=Gray}Just as I thought. My spellsongs won't be as effective\non this man...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_106_m01_032: {SetColor=Gray}Tch. How did I end up with this joke for a...a... Ugh.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV14_106_m01_018: Anyway, if you don't mind... I have a few questions\nI'd like to ask you now.
MID_EV14_106_m01_019: Considering you can't do much to stop me, now\nseems like a good time to get the answers I want.
MID_EV14_106_m01_020: Ngh— What the hell?! Get back!
MID_EV14_106_m01_021: Shenlo! You are the last person I expected to come\nto my rescue.
MID_EV14_106_m01_022: I have been tracking you at the request of\nMagistra Raksha.
MID_EV14_106_m01_023: It is dangerous here. We must withdraw.\nCome with me.
MID_EV14_106_m01_024: I...appreciate the assistance. I suppose I am in your\ndebt now.
MID_EV14_106_m01_025: They escaped? Oh well. I'm sure there will be more\nopportunities for questions later.
MID_EV14_106_m01_026: Talimun...I'm starting to wonder...
MID_EV14_106_m01_027: What's this? Figuring out what a great guy I am?\nAnd wondering what? If I'd take you to dinner?
MID_EV14_106_m01_028: No! My gods, you're shameless. It's just...I'm a bit\nsurprised, that's all.
MID_EV14_038_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV14_038_m01_001: And she's gone. The list of questions I'd like to ask\nher grows longer and longer.
MID_EV14_038_m01_041: 
MID_EV14_038_m01_002: No doubt she's the woman who smells of ambergris\nfrom the southern sea.
MID_EV14_038_m01_003: Lechner. I so very much wanted to choke the life out\nof you with my own hands.
MID_EV14_038_m01_004: That was the last one. Everyone named in the\nMahdel List is dead. Still...
MID_EV14_038_m01_006: I sympathize with you, Leilidahna, but you must\nshake this off.
MID_EV14_038_m01_007: Time is of the essence.
MID_EV14_038_m01_008: And you still want to take your revenge on Bertrand,\ndo you not?
MID_EV14_038_m01_009: Besides, now that we have the carriage, the real\nenemy is sure to make their move.
MID_EV14_038_m01_010: So, let us open up this carriage and see what kind of\nmysterious cargo awaits inside.
MID_EV14_038_m01_011: You're right. Of course...you're right.
MID_EV14_038_m01_012: Hey, is this...gold?! Look...there's so much!
MID_EV14_038_m01_013: No, this is far more extraordinary than gold.
MID_EV14_038_m01_014: This is refined orichalcum. To see such a large\nquantity of it is unheard of.
MID_EV14_038_m01_015: Well, well. There's something you don't see in every\nmysterious ghost carriage... Orichalcum!
MID_EV14_038_m01_016: And one hell of a hoard, I must say.
MID_EV14_038_m01_017: Stop right there. You don't really think I'm gonna\nsplit this with you, do you?
MID_EV14_038_m01_018: Of course not. I won't pretend I'm not interested in it.\nBut it'd be too much to handle, even for me.
MID_EV14_038_m01_019: Orichalcum is a rare metal. The moment I go to\nsell it, they'll come looking for me.
MID_EV14_038_m01_020: I could try selling it overseas to Fódlan, but not many\nof their artisans know how to work it.
MID_EV14_038_m01_021: Wouldn't fetch much.
MID_EV14_038_m01_022: No, if anything, I could take it somewhere over\nby Morfis...
MID_EV14_038_m01_023: But even then, I risk inspection at the port.\nThey'd arrest us on the spot.
MID_EV14_038_m01_024: Carrying something like that is asking for trouble.
MID_EV14_038_m01_025: Part of me loves the idea, but I'll have to let it lie\nfor now. And so, I'll be going.
MID_EV14_038_m01_026: He was...lively. Is he really just some merchant?
MID_EV14_038_m01_027: Whatever he is, he did come to our aid. We ought\nto be grateful for that at least.
MID_EV14_038_m01_028: Time to get back to the topic at hand, yes?
MID_EV14_038_m01_029: Considering the route traveled by the\nghost carriage...
MID_EV14_038_m01_030: it seems likely this orichalcum was taken from the\nCoris Mine, refined, and dispatched to Dagsion.
MID_EV14_038_m01_031: What? The Coris Mine? But Balboa is dead.
MID_EV14_038_m01_032: They must have replaced her. I bet it didn't\ntake them long either.
MID_EV14_038_m01_033: Seems likely. It must have happened right after all\nthe chaos erupted.
MID_EV14_038_m01_034: I have no doubt Arago employed harsh measures\nto quell the riots.
MID_EV14_038_m01_035: They probably moved quickly to get the mining\noperation up and running again.
MID_EV14_038_m01_036: Sounds about right. I'm sure the people of Kassite\nsaw a great deal of spilled blood yet again.
MID_EV14_038_m01_037: But...no... Those people barely had a chance to\ncelebrate their freedom...
MID_EV14_038_m01_038: Tch...
MID_EV14_038_m01_039: I'll find a place to hide this carriage and its\ndangerous cargo.
MID_EV14_038_m01_040: Then let's head back to Dagsion and wait there for\nthe enemy to make their move.